[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3721594240","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/114713#issuecomment-3721594240","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/114713","id":3721594240,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7d0wWA","user":{"login":"kleonc","id":9283098,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjkyODMwOTg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/9283098?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc","html_url":"https://github.com/kleonc","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-01-08T02:12:56Z","updated_at":"2026-01-08T02:18:54Z","body":"The change is intended, I've done this in #113988 as a bugfix:\n\n> #86983 changed only `AStar2D::get_id_path`/`AStar3D::get_id_path` to return an empty path if `from` point is disabled.\n\n(#86983 was merged in `4.5.beta1`)\n\nNow all AStar classes should be behave consistently in case \"from\" point is disabled.\nNote that relevant methods' documentation are updated to mention this (line 82 below).\nhttps://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/5d9722e83288f33827bcad70561f0737f8cde456/doc/classes/AStarGrid2D.xml#L75-L85\n\n> This is different from the behaviour that appears to be present from 4.5 through 4.6 beta2 with no indication in the beta3 release notes that a relevant area has been modified.\n\nI've just linked the production team about this issue (so the blog post will likely get updated to mention the change).\n\n---\n\nNote that if you want the previous behavior it's as simple as enabling given `from` point temporarily:\n```gdscript\nvar is_from_solid: bool = astar.is_point_solid(from)\nastar.set_point_solid(from, false)\n\nvar path = astar.get_id_path(from, ...)\n\nastar.set_point_solid(from, is_from_solid) # Restore previous state.\n```","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3721594240/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3721626193","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/114713#issuecomment-3721626193","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/114713","id":3721626193,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7d04JR","user":{"login":"davidbragg","id":1179514,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjExNzk1MTQ=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1179514?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/davidbragg","html_url":"https://github.com/davidbragg","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davidbragg/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davidbragg/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davidbragg/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davidbragg/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davidbragg/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davidbragg/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davidbragg/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davidbragg/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davidbragg/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-01-08T02:29:23Z","updated_at":"2026-01-08T02:29:23Z","body":"I thought it might be intentional. When I couldn't find any indication for it being fixed I logged it just in case. Thank you for confirming. I'm closing this out now.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3721626193/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]